abstract: >-
  A numerically robust, cubic-convergent solver based on Halley's
  method for the nonlinear chord-length residual formulation of the
  clothoid (Euler spiral) G^1 Hermite interpolation problem. Operates
  directly on the arc-length parameter L using fixed 32-point
  Gauss-Legendre quadrature for the six moment integrals that define
  the residual f(L) and its first two analytic derivatives. The four
  primitive integral derivatives and the residual second-derivative
  identity are machine-checked in Coq using the Coquelicot
  real-analysis library, with no Admitted lemmas. Production-grade
  reference implementations in Python, C# (.NET 8), Java 21, and
  TypeScript (Node.js) are bit-identical to within 1e-9 m on every
  case of a 9,058-record benchmark corpus drawn from the public
  ProRail Spoorgeometrie railway-geometry dataset.

